<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Resource-shrinker keep rules for SynthBox.

  The release build runs the R8 resource shrinker (see
  build/app/outputs/mapping/release/resources.txt). It decides reachability by
  scanning bytecode and XML for resource *references*. Every drawable below is
  referenced only from Dart, as a string, on the platform channel:

      MediaControl.custom(androidIcon: 'drawable/ic_shuffle_on', ...)
      AudioServiceConfig(androidNotificationIcon: 'drawable/ic_stat_synthbox')

  Flutter's Dart AOT snapshot is opaque to the shrinker, so it classified all of
  them as unreachable and stripped them out of the release APK entirely:

      @io.github.zhaoymovo.ffs:drawable/ic_shuffle_on : reachable=false

  At runtime com.ryanheise.audioservice.AudioService resolves those names with
  Resources.getIdentifier(...), which returns 0 once the resource is gone. A
  small-icon resource id of 0 makes NotificationCompat.Builder.build() throw, so
  buildNotification() never returns and startForeground() never posts anything.
  Android 11+ derives the Quick Settings / lock-screen media card from that
  notification, so the observable symptom is that the system media controls
  NEVER appear — even though the MediaSession itself is created and activated
  correctly, and even though audio keeps playing.

  Do not remove these entries, and add one for every new icon that Dart names as
  a string. A Dart-only reference is invisible to the shrinker.
-->
<resources xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools"
    tools:keep="@drawable/ic_shuffle_on,@drawable/ic_shuffle_off,@drawable/ic_repeat_one,@drawable/ic_repeat_all,@drawable/ic_repeat_none,@drawable/ic_stat_synthbox" />
